# Krezk's people at the Pool of the White Sun (lane 28, 2026-10-08: "more people walking around and doing things"):
# Widow Catrina lighting her candle at the water, and Old Simion keeping the graves. Unvoiced for now.

~ mourner
Widow Catrina: Every morning I tell him the news. The goats, the weather, who's fallen out with whom. The water never freezes, not even in the deep of winter. That's how I know he hears.
-> mourner_menu

~ mourner_menu
* [if not flag.catrina_told] [Insight DC 13] (Ask gently whether the water ever answers.) -> mourner_secret | mourner_miss
* Good day. -> END

~ mourner_secret
set catrina_told
Widow Catrina [sad]: Five years I've told that water what the hens laid and who took ill, never expecting a word back.
Widow Catrina [afraid]: Then last month the ripples stopped, and a voice from the bottom said thank you for the news. A young man's voice.
Widow Catrina: It wasn't my Nicolae's voice, and I haven't breathed a word of it to a living soul.
-> mourner_menu

~ mourner_miss
Narrator: Widow Catrina tests the dark water with two fingers, tells you only that the pool is cold today, and turns back to her basket.
-> mourner_menu

~ grave_keeper
if flag.sorin_fate == "pool"
Old Simion [sad]: The Krezkov boy, at peace in the water at last. I'll keep his stone straighter than all the rest. Don't tell the others.
-> keeper_menu
endif
Old Simion: Stone suns, every one, so they face the morning. The snow pushes them crooked. I push them back. Between us we've kept it up for thirty years.
-> keeper_menu

~ keeper_menu
* What would you like, Simion? -> keeper_want
* [if flag.simion_want_heard] That stone with no name, at the end of the row? -> keeper_secret
* Good day. -> END

~ keeper_want
set simion_want_heard
Old Simion: Seventy stones by the water, and I know the name and the last words under every one of them.
Old Simion [sad]: I only wish someone younger had the patience to stand in the cold and learn them before I forget.
-> keeper_menu

~ keeper_secret
Narrator: At the end of the row stands a blank sun-stone beside a neat, deep trench covered with pine boughs to keep the drift out.
Old Simion: Ground freezes hard as iron come midwinter, so I dug my own while my back still had the bend in it.
-> keeper_menu
